course: dictionary
lesson: 15891
title: Uniquely: one of a kind
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unique means one of a kind. Something is unique when nothing else is quite like it. Add -ly and you get uniquely, which tells you how something is done or how it is. «The pattern on the shell is uniquely its own, found on no other shell.» The shell has one pattern that no other shell has.
explain: Uniquely can also mean especially or particularly. «The tool is uniquely designed for left-handed people.» Here it does not mean only one of its kind. It means the tool was made especially well for left-handed people. Read the words around it to see which meaning fits.
explain: Use the swap check. Put your meaning in place of the word and see if the sentence still makes sense. «The shell is in a way that is the only one of its kind, found on no other shell» works. If your meaning does not fit, try the other one.
fact: «Uniquely» means in a way that is the only one of its kind.
fact: «Uniquely» can also mean especially or particularly, as in «uniquely suited».
fact: Fingerprints identify people uniquely, because each person's fingerprints are their own.
fact: Some animals live uniquely on one island, which means they are found nowhere else.
fact: In maths, a number can be written uniquely as a product of primes, which means there is only one way to write it that way.
exercise: «The painting is uniquely hers, and nobody else has painted anything like it.» What does uniquely mean? | In a copied way, like everyone else | Very quickly | Sadly and slowly | *In a way that is the only one of its kind
exercise: «This tool is uniquely designed for left-handed people.» What does uniquely mean here? | Once a year | *Especially, made with this one purpose in mind | Loudly, for everyone to hear | Carelessly
exercise: Nadia says «uniquely» is just another word for «oddly». Is she right? | Yes, the two words mean exactly the same | Yes, it means strangely | Yes, it means quickly | *No, uniquely means the only one of its kind
test: «The old clock was uniquely made, with no other like it in the world.» What does uniquely mean? | In a way that is slow to start | In a way that is very noisy | In a way that is cheap and common | *In a way that is the only one of its kind
test: A maths book says a number can be written uniquely as a product of primes. What does uniquely mean here? | Many different ways | Without any primes | *Only one way | Very fast
exam: Which sentence uses uniquely to mean the only one of its kind? | Ben ran uniquely fast | We ate uniquely cake for tea | *The pattern on the shell is uniquely its own, found on no other shell | The bus came uniquely late
